0..56 Comment "// `G` after `F` acts on a path as their composite does."
57..59 Comment "//"
60..132 Comment "// The kernel re-derives what the checker accepts at a reflexivity whose"
133..166 Comment "// endpoint reads through a bind."
167..169 Comment "//"
170..246 Comment "// Based path induction proves it. At reflexivity both actions reduce to the"
247..324 Comment "// reflexivity at `G(F(x))`. The composite\'s action reads through its bind to"
325..405 Comment "// the call `G(⟨F(x)⟩)`, which the other side holds. The functions stated as"
406..480 Comment "// lambdas read the same way: composing with `g`, then with `h`, acts on a"
481..514 Comment "// square as composing with both."
515..517 Comment "//"
518..590 Comment "// - see: #3969 — the kernel\'s reading of an endpoint through its bind"
591..670 Comment "// - see: `then-units-in-the-kernel.gandr` — reflexivity\'s units under `then`"
671..733 Comment "// - see: `transport-dependent.gandr` — based path induction"
735..802 Comment "/// A function\'s action on a path, whose type states its endpoints."
